1
00:03:16,363 --> 00:03:22,363
The magic of friendship never changes.

2
00:06:32,727 --> 00:06:38,727
My Little Pony: Equestria Girls is a animation, comedy,
family film directed by Jayson Thiessen.

3
00:09:49,090 --> 00:09:55,090
Via a magic mirror, Twilight Sparkle travels into an alternate universe in
order to recover a crown that was stolen from the Crystal Empire.

4
00:13:05,454 --> 00:13:11,454
Upon her arrival she is horrified to learn that she has turned into a human.

5
00:16:21,818 --> 00:16:27,818
Twilight Sparkle (voice), played by Tara Strong.

6
00:19:38,181 --> 00:19:44,181
Applejack / Rainbow Dash (voice), played by Ashleigh Ball.

7
00:22:54,545 --> 00:23:00,545
Pinkie Pie / Fluttershy (voice), played by Andrea Libman.

8
00:26:10,909 --> 00:26:16,909
Rarity / Princess Luna / Vice Principal Luna / Cup Cake
(voice), played by Tabitha St. Germain.

9
00:29:27,272 --> 00:29:33,272
Spike (voice), played by Cathy Weseluck.

10
00:32:43,636 --> 00:32:49,636
Sunset Shimmer (voice) / Twilight Sparkle  (singing
voice), played by Rebecca Shoichet.

11
00:36:00,000 --> 00:36:06,000
My Little Pony: Equestria Girls is a 2013 animated musical fantasy film directed by Jayson Thiessen, written by
Meghan McCarthy, and produced by DHX Media Vancouver for Hasbro Studios in the United States.

12
00:39:16,363 --> 00:39:22,363
It is the first installment in Hasbro's Equestria Girls franchise, which serves as
an anthropomorphic spin-off to the 2010 relaunch of My Little Pony.

13
00:42:32,727 --> 00:42:38,727
The film and franchise's introduction also commemorates the 30th
anniversary of the original My Little Pony toy line.

14
00:45:49,090 --> 00:45:55,090
Equestria Girls re-envisions the main characters of its parent franchise, normally
ponies, as teenage humanoid characters in a high school setting.

15
00:49:05,454 --> 00:49:11,454
Set between the third and fourth seasons of the My Little Pony: Friendship Is Magic television series, the plot involves
Twilight Sparkle pursuing her stolen crown into an alternate world, where she transforms into a humanoid teenage girl.

16
00:52:21,818 --> 00:52:27,818
While learning how to behave locally, Twilight encounters the parallel universe
counterparts of her pony friends, who join her in the search for her crown.

17
00:55:38,181 --> 00:55:44,181
My Little Pony: Equestria Girls premiered at the Los Angeles Film Festival on June 15, 2013, and entered limited
release in the United States and Canada on June 16, followed by a home media release on August 6.

18
00:58:54,545 --> 00:59:00,545
The film received mixed reviews, with most criticism directed at the
character design, writing, plot, and characterization.

19
01:02:10,909 --> 01:02:16,909
It was followed by three sequels, Rainbow Rocks (2014), Friendship Games (2015) and
Legend of Everfree (2016) – all of which were more positively received.

20
01:05:27,272 --> 01:05:33,272
The film explores themes of princess, high school, friendship, magic, villain.

21
01:08:43,636 --> 01:08:49,636
The tone is lighthearted.
